  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest result to date is config_006 (RNA-only, multi-profile, scVI n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. RNA encoders rank clearly: scVI n200 > PCA n2000 > scGPT. Image-only with ResNet50 is very weak (0.208), but ViT-L has not been tested at all. The central unresolved question is whether the image modality can add value on top of the strong RNA baseline, and whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) changes that picture. This experiment (config_038) pairs the proven-best RNA setup (scVI n200, multi-profile, transformer aggregation) with the strongest available image encoder (ViT-L) and the simplest fusion (concat), isolating the question 'does a strong image representation add complementary signal?' If it beats 0.653, image modality is confirmed useful and we can explore fusion strategies; if it does not, we can rule out image as a useful modality and concentrate remaining budget on RNA-side refinements. This is the highest-information single step because it directly tests the largest unexplored design axis (multimodal fusion) while holding all RNA-side choices at their known-optimal values."
}

